                    <h2 id="teacher-daily-plan-activities-PATCHapi-teacher-teacher-daily-plan--id--status">Update activity execution status.</h2>

<p>
</p>

<p>Allows the teacher to mark an activity as executed or not_executed.
The frontend sends a PATCH with the new status value.</p>

<span id="example-requests-PATCHapi-teacher-teacher-daily-plan--id--status">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request PATCH \
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/teacher/teacher/daily-plan/10/status" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"status\": \"executed\",
    \"plan_day_id\": 5,
    \"planning_label\": \"2025\\/2026\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/teacher/teacher/daily-plan/10/status"
);

const headers = {
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "status": "executed",
    "plan_day_id": 5,
    "planning_label": "2025\/2026"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "PATCH",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

